abstract:
The bivariate series $	heta (q,x):=\sum _{j=0}^{\infty}q^{j(j+1)/2}x^j$ defines a {\em partial theta function}. For fixed $q$ ($|q|<1$), $	heta (q,.)$ is an entire function. We prove a property of stabilization of the coefficients of the Laurent series in $q$ of the zeros of $	heta$. The coefficients $r_k$ of the stabilized series are positive integers. They are the elements of a known increasing sequence satisfying the recurrence relation $r_k=\sum _{
u =1}^{\infty}(-1)^{
u -1}(2
u +1)r_{k-
u (
u +1)/2}$.
